  "body": "The specification for playbackRate uses language that seems very loose and possibly open to wide interpretation. It says that the user agent must mute the element when the audio playback is not useful. Useful to whom? In what way? Does sample rate factor in?  \r\n\r\nIt also says if the element's playbackRate is not 1.0, the user agent may apply pitch adjustments to the audio as necessary to render it faithfully.  \r\n\r\nHow does the user agent determine useful or faithful playback? I'm kind of surprised that browser vendors haven't asked. Or maybe they're too busy copying each other?\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#dom-media-playbackrate",
